        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Some writers and editors avoid the first person by using the passive everywhere, but deleting an / or we doesn't make a researcher's thinking more objective. We know that behind those impersonal sentences are still flesh-and-blood people doing, thinking, and writing. In fact, the first-person / and we are common in scholarly prose when used with verbs that name actions unique to the writer.",
            "block_bbox": [
                128,
                383,
                783,
                501
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
